{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788689815080,"sessionID":"ses_f89c7c6c8ffejbZzDUSP7ct9OM","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-beba0c021e8bb007","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 6 2>/dev/null; echo \"===\"; git log --all --oneline | head -30"},"output":"title:\tFront-end cleanups from the typed-streams review\nstate:\tCLOSED\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t6\n--\nStyle/standards findings from the issue-4 review — all judgement calls, none blocking, consolidated here rather than blocking the merge:\n\n- `check.rs` `rebase()`: base-splitting block verbatim-triplicated across Field/Unwrap/Index arms; also returns `(Tir, Tir)` distinguished only by position — a `Rebased { body, source }` struct.\n- `check.rs` `access()`: grew to `(Tir, Type, usize, bool)` with an unnamed trailing bool — name the struct.\n- Reserved builtin type names (\"Vec\"/\"Opt\"/\"Stream\") now live in three places (`enum_map`, `alias_map`, `parse.rs`) — one `RESERVED_TYPE_NAMES` const + `is_builtin_type_name`.\n- `check_linear`'s `what` parameter carries a dangling-\"and\" message fragment — restructure the message assembly.\n- `collect`'s typing rule exists twice (synth and expect paths) with divergent error quality — extract one helper.\n- `tests/streaming.rs`: `spawn_go/py/js` are one body with three parameters — extract `spawn_interpreted`; `tests/streams.rs`: group the ~20 flat tests into `mod` blocks per concern (containment / linearity / sources).\n- Minor: `LinearViolation::Branches(usize, usize)` named fields; duplicated `in_mapper` ctx setup; inline jsonlines-sink block in `check()` wants extraction.\n\nGood candidates for one /simplify pass; behavior-neutral throughout.\n===\n9897054 board: archive three already-landed rows missed by the land pipeline\n8cba7d0 Merg