                        45c76be [issue-159]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-169                                                      d9896ec [issue-169]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177                                                      de58ffc [issue-177]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-93                                                       7c4cc86 [issue-93]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build                           8011893 [issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build                                    8011893 [issue-benchmark-fasta-build]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-suite-build                                    f74a274 [issue-benchmark-suite-build]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-draft-core-model-migration                               8cba7d0 [issue-draft-core-model-migration]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-c-escalation                                 298823d [issue-float-build-c-escalation]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-go                                           86c03af [issue-float-build-go]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-jq                                           298823d [issue-float-build-jq]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-lua                                          5e2fd24 [issue-float-build-lua]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python                                       8f602b6 [issue-float-build-python]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-rust                                         35f0748 [issue-float-build-rust]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-recursive-descent-order-research                         945cf81 [issue-recursive-descent-order-research]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stdout-stderr-effect-model-research                      b3c4bb7 [issue-stdout-stderr-effect-model-research]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation 6bc040d [issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation]\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fasta-build-investigation          6bc040d [issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fasta-build-investigation]\n---LANE---\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x   2 kantord kantord    40 Sep  6 10:27 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 405 root    root    13740 Sep  6 12:17 ..\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"ls plans/incidents/ | grep -i fannkuch; echo \"---WORKTREES---\"; git worktree list; echo \"---LANE---\"; ls -la /tmp/opencode 2>/dev/null; find / -maxdepth 4 -name \"*fannkuch*\" -type d 2>/dev/null","time":{"start":1788689822650,"end":1788689822844}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The incident directory for fannkuch-redux doesn't appear in the list... let me look. The incidents listed are: issue-140, 149, 152, 153, 158, 159, 168, 169, 170, 172, 174, 177, float-build-go/lua/python/rust, float-format-research, http-query-sugar-research, param-destructure-build, recursive-descent-order-research, search-layer-build. \n\nThere's no issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build incident directory yet? Wait the task says \"evidence frozen in plans/incidents/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-20260906/\". Let me look. The date is 20260906. Let me list incidents with that date. Actually the incident dirs are like \"issue-177-20260903\". Let me check the fannkuch ones. Hmm I don't see any fannkuch. Let me look for the lane.\n\nActually, the task says read the incident evidence AND the lane worktree. Let me find the lane worktree. The lane is \"issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build\". Let me look for the git worktree.\n\nAlso there's a LAND-FAILURE.txt and ESCALATION.md at root. Let me read those.\n\nLet me look at the incident directory - maybe it doesn't exist yet and I need to find the evidence elsewhere. Let me search.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_07638b14f001BenwVeHG7WYsKo","sessionID":"ses_f89c7c6c8ffejbZzDUSP7ct9OM","messageID":"msg_07638963b0016e7NUOUDLDnPTO"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788689823205,"sessionID":"ses_f89c7c6c8ffejbZzDUSP7ct9OM","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9b39a422b11c823d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation/ESCALATION.md"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation/ESCALATION.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Escalation: `just check` cannot go green as root\n2: \n3: ## Question\n4: \n5: The `search-layer-build` brief requires `just check` green. Two pre-existing tests,\n6: `tests/fmt_project.rs::unreadable_directory_is_reported_and_walk_continues` and\n7: `::unreadable_file_is_reported_and_walk_continues`, cannot pass when the suite runs as root:\n8: they chmod a directory or file to `0o000` and assert that the `toylang fmt` walker reports a\n9: permission error. Root bypasses permission bits, so `read_dir`/`read` succeed and the refusal\n10: never happens.\n11: \n12: ## Evidence it is environmental, not caused by this branch\n13: \n14: - The failing assertion is exactly `read_dir` on a `0o000` directory. Verified in this sandbox:\n15:   as root, `ls` reads the directory; as `nobody` (via `setpriv`), it gets `Permission denied`.\n16: - Running the already-built `fmt_project` test binary as `nobody` passes both tests unchanged.\n17: - CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs on `ubuntu-latest`, a non-root user, where both pass.\n18: \n19: None of this branch's changes (the `first`/`any`/`all` builtins) touch file permissions or the\n20: formatter.\n21: \n22: ## Alternatives\n23: \n24: 1. **Skip the two tests when running as root.** Minimal, transparent, keeps the assertions\n25:    fully active for the non-root case that CI and normal development run. The chosen path.\n26: 2. **Run the whole suite as a non-root user in this sandbox.** Requires giving a non-root user\n27:    write access to `/repo` (the suite rewrites `tests/corpus/*.yaml` and\n28:    `site/public/corpus.json` in place) and a copy of `CARGO_HOME`; invasive and fragile.\n29: 3. **Leave `just check` red and document only.** Fails the brief's explicit definition of done.\n30: \n31: ## Decision\n32: \n33: Took alternative 1: a `running_as_root()` guard (`id -u` reports 0) at the top of the two\n34: tests, with a comment explaining why the assertion is unobservable as root. The guard does not\n35: silently cover a broken walker: for any non-root user the tests run exactly as before. Revert\n36: this if the maintainer prefers a different accommodation.\n\n(End of file - total 36 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Escalation: `just check` cannot go green as root\n\n## Question\n\nThe `search-layer-build` brief requires `just check` green. Two pre-existing tests,\n`tests/fmt_project.rs::unreadable_directory_is_reported_and_walk_continues` and\n`::unreadable_file_is_reported_and_walk_continues`, cannot pass when the suite runs as root:\nthey chmod a directory or file to `0o000` and assert that the `toylang fmt` walker reports a\npermission error. Root bypasses permission bits, so `read_dir`/`read` succeed and the refusal\nnever happens.\n\n## Evidence it is environmental, not caused by this branch\n\n- The failing assertion is exactly `read_dir` on a `0o000` directory. Verified in this sandbox:\n  as root, `ls` reads the directory; as `nobody` (via `setpriv`), it gets `Permission denied`.\n- Running the already-built `fmt_project` test binary as `nobody` passes both tests unchanged.\n- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs on `ubuntu-latest`, a non-root user, where both pass.\n\nNone of this branch's changes (the `first`/`any`/`all` builtins) touch file permissions or the\nformatter.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation/ESCALATION.md","text":"# Escalation: `just check` cannot go green as root\n\n## Question\n\nThe `search-layer-build` brief requires `just check` green. Two pre-existing tests,\n`tests/fmt_project.rs::unreadable_directory_is_reported_and_walk_continues` and\n`::unreadable_file_is_reported_and_walk_continues`, cannot pass when the suite runs as root:\nthey chmod a directory or file to `0o000` and assert that the `toylang fmt` walker reports a\npermission error. Root bypasses permission bits, so `read_dir`/`read` succeed and the refusal\nnever happens.\n\n## Evidence it is environmental, not caused by this branch\n\n- The failing assertion is exactly `read_dir` on a `0o000` directory. Verified in this sandbox:\n  as root, `ls` reads the directory; as `nobody` (via `setpriv`), it gets `Permission denied`.\n- Running the already-built `fmt_project` test binary as `nobody` passes both tests unchanged.\n- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs on `ubuntu-latest`, a non-root user, where both pass.\n\nNone of this branch's changes (the `first`/`any`/`all` builtins) touch file permissions or the\nformatter.\n\n## Alternatives\n\n1. **Skip the two tests when running as root.** Minimal, transparent, keeps the assertions\n   fully active for the non-root case that CI and normal development run. The chosen path.\n2. **Run the whole suite as a non-root user in this sandbox.** Requires giving a non-root user\n   write access to `/repo` (the suite rewrites `tests/corpus/*.yaml` and\n   `site/public/corpus.json` in place) and a copy of `CARGO_HOME`; invasive and fragile.\n3. **Leave `just check` red and document only.** Fails the brief's explicit definition of done.\n\n## Decision\n\nTook alternative 1: a `running_as_root()` guard (`id -u` reports 0) at the top of the two\ntests, with a comment explaining why the assertion is unobservable as root. The guard does not\nsilently cover a broken walker: for any non-root user the tests run exactly as before. Revert\nthis if the maintainer prefers a different accommodation.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":36,"totalLines":36,"truncated":false}},"title":"ESCALATION.md","time":{"start":1788689823195,"end":1788689823203}},"id":"prt_07638b3b30012twN5hjkKh8Q23","sessionID":"ses_f89c7c6c8ffejbZzDUSP7ct9OM","messageID":"msg_07638963b0016e7NUOUDLDnPTO"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788689823639,"sessionID":"ses_f89c7c6c8ffejbZzDUSP7ct9OM","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a8730977cb91bd96","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation/LAND-FAILURE.txt"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation/LAND-FAILURE.txt</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Resolved: origin/main merged into issue-172 (landing attempt 2). The eight\n2: conflicts were all additive or test-syntax clashes, resolved in favor of the\n3: feature's intent:\n4: \n5: - build.rs, src/tags.rs, src/tir.rs: both the feature's `parse` builtin and\n6:   main's `first`/`any`/`all` kept.\n7: - src/check/mod.rs: BUILTIN_NAMES grew to 20 (16 ancestor + parse + first/any/all).\n8: - site/public/corpus.json: regenerated by the export_site test.\n9: - tests/backend_js.rs, tests/corpus/record_result.yaml, tests/step_5.rs: kept the\n10:   feature's stdin source as `pick(parse(stdin))` -- main had renamed the\n11:   record-returning function to `pick` (to dodge its new `first` builtin), and the\n12:   feature retires `input`, so the call became `pick(parse(stdin))` instead of\n13:   main's stale `pick(input)`.\n14: \n15: `just check` from the worktree root: 361 passed, 2 skipped (the docs mega-test\n16: excluded from check, and the ignored euler_real_data tier). The go_streams\n17: failures recorded on the earlier attempt no longer reproduce.\n\n(End of file - total 17 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Resolved: origin/main merged into issue-172 (landing attempt 2). The eight\nconflicts were all additive or test-syntax clashes, resolved in favor of the\nfeature's intent:\n\n- build.rs, src/tags.rs, src/tir.rs: both the feature's `parse` builtin and\n  main's `first`/`any`/`all` kept.\n- src/check/mod.rs: BUILTIN_NAMES grew to 20 (16 ancestor + parse + first/any/all).\n- site/public/corpus.json: regenerated by the export_site test.\n- tests/backend_js.rs, tests/corpus/record_result.yaml, tests/step_5.rs: kept the\n  feature's stdin source as `pick(parse(stdin))` -- main had renamed the\n  record-returning function to `pick` (to dodge its new `first` builtin), and the\n  feature retires `input`, so the call became `pick(parse(stdin))` instead of\n  main's stale `pick(input)`.\n\n`just check` from the worktree root: 361 passed, 2 skipped (the docs mega-test\nexcluded from check, and the ignored euler_real_data tier). The go_streams\nfailures recorded on the earlier attempt no longer reproduce.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-stuck-issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build-investigation/LAND-FAILURE.txt","text":"Resolved: origin/main merged into issue-172 (landing attempt 2). The eight\nconflicts were all additive or test-syntax clashes, resolved in favor of the\nfeature's intent:\n\n- build.rs, src/tags.rs, src/tir.rs: both the feature's `parse` builtin and\n  main's `first`/`any`/`all` kept.\n- src/check/mod.rs: BUILTIN_NAMES grew to 20 (16 ancestor + parse + first/any/all).\n- site/public/corpus.json: regenerated by the export_site test.\n- tests/backend_js.rs, tests/corpus/record_result.yaml, tests/step_5.rs: kept the\n  feature's stdin source as `pick(parse(stdin))` -- main had renamed the\n  record-returning function to `pick` (to dodge its new `first` builtin), and the\n  feature retires `input`, so the call became `pick(parse(stdin))` instead of\n  main's stale `pick(input)`.\n\n`just check` from the worktree root: 361 passed, 2 skipped (the docs mega-test\nexcluded from check, and the ignored euler_real_data tier). The go_streams\nfailures recorded on the earlier attempt no longer reproduce.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":17,"totalLines":17,"truncated":false}},"title":"LAND-FAILURE.txt","time":{"start":1788689823632,"end":1788689823637}},"id":"prt_07638b5de001meE04OLO3rZSU2","sessionID":"ses_f89c7c6c8ffejbZzDUSP7ct9OM","messageID":"msg_07638963b0016e7NUOUDLDnPTO"}}
